# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "The toml and ini fence arms split: each includes its own private grammar"

# `toml` includes the vendored, private source.toml.tw5-syntax (TOML 1.1: the \e and \xHH
# escapes, optional seconds, and a quoted-dotted table-header key held as one segment). `ini`
# includes VS Code's own source.ini, a CONTROL proving each arm reads through its own grammar.

```toml
[fruit."var.ies"]
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.embedded.block.toml source.toml.tw5-syntax
#          ^ meta.section.toml entity.name.section.toml
lt2 = 14:15
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.embedded.block.toml source.toml.tw5-syntax
#      ^^^^^ constant.other.time.toml
esc = "e\e x\x61"
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.embedded.block.toml source.toml.tw5-syntax
#       ^^ constant.character.escape.toml
#           ^^^^ constant.character.escape.unicode.8bit.toml
```

```ini
; a comment, not invalid
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.embedded.block.ini source.ini punctuation.definition.comment.ini
[section]
key=value
```
